  "raw_policy_excerpt": "Program: Atlassian | URL: https://bugcrowd.com/engagements/atlassian | safe_harbor: full | allows_disclosure: false | managed_by_bugcrowd: true | max_payout: 12000\n\nSource: arkadiyt/bounty-targets-data bugcrowd_data.json (2026-05-17)\n\nNOTABLE SCOPE RULES (from dump):\n- Test only your OWN instances: 'Any customer instance. Do not test customer instances or affect customer data. Customer cloud instances may be in the form of <customer>.atlassian.net or <customer>.jira.com. Test only your own instances.'\n- 'Any repository that you are not an owner of - do not impact Atlassian customers in any way.'\n- Marketplace apps (first and third party) are excluded from this program but may be in scope at https://bugcrowd.com/atlassianapps\n- Out of scope: Any internal or development services, shop.atlassian.com, bytebucket.org, *.bitbucket.io, blog.bitbucket.org, HipChat, Stride, support.atlassian.com, support.loom.com, info.loom.com\n\nIN-SCOPE HIGHLIGHTS:\n- Atlassian Guard, Admin (admin.atlassian.com), Identity (id.atlassian.com)\n- Bitbucket Cloud (bitbucket.org) including Pipelines\n- Confluence Cloud, Jira Software/Service Management/Work Management Cloud (via own test instances)\n- *.atlassian.com and *.atl-paas.net (both directly and indirectly exploitable from *.atlassian.net)\n- *.atlastunnel.com\n- *.loom.com, Loom Desktop (Win/macOS), Loom Android/iOS, Loom Chrome Extension\n- Rovo, Rovo Dev CLI, Atlassian MCP Server (mcp.atlassian.com)\n- Compass, Atlas, Marketplace, Bamboo, Crucible, FishEye, Sourcetree\n- Data Center products: Bitbucket DC, Confluence DC, Crowd, Jira Core DC, Jira Service Management DC, Jira Software DC\n- Mobile apps: Confluence Cloud/DC (Android+iOS), Jira Cloud/DC (Android+iOS), Loom (Android+iOS)\n- Forge Platform, GraphQL API, Forge CLI (@forge/cli npm), Confluence Companion App\n- Catch-all: 'Other - (all other Atlassian targets)'\n- Jira Product Discovery"
